## Learned Rules

<!-- Append below; same format as 000-core-rules.mdc. Number sequentially within this file. -->

1. [UX] Use `@radix-ui/react-*` for complex interactive UI (Switch, Progress, Dialog, Select, Tabs). For plain text entry, use native HTML inputs/textareas styled with Tailwind and wired to a Radix **Label** for accessibility.
2. [ARCH] Feature encapsulation: feature root `index.ts` barrel files export only the **public API** (pages, shared types, global actions). Do not export internal-only pieces (feature-local forms, cells, tables).
3. [CODE] Treat **strict TypeScript** and **strict ESLint** as the bar: fix lint in touched modules; prefer narrowing and explicit types over `any`, loose assertions, and unnecessary non-null assertions (`!`).
4. [PROCESS] Zero-warning policy: do not ship unused variables, empty interfaces, or unresolved `react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` warnings in code you change.
5. [ARCH] `frontend/proxy.ts` (edge middleware) controls auth: **do not** treat `/` as a protected route — it is the public marketing site. Redirect authenticated users away from auth pages to `/dashboard`, not `/`.
6. [ARCH] `SessionMonitor` must not treat “no server session” as session expiry for anonymous users. Emit `rutalink:session-expired` only when `isAuthenticated()` (client `user_info` cookie) is true, or skip monitoring on `/` and auth routes — otherwise guests calling `/api/auth/session` see `authenticated: false` and get sent to `/login` incorrectly.
